    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420">

                <pb facs="0540" n="282" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg282"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1406</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 246]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 3, 1915</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 26.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that because of
                    the complaints made by the Swedish Government concerning the delay and
                    difficulties of traffic as a result of the measures adopted by the English, the
                    British Government has sent a commission to Sweden to try to come to some
                    understanding in the matter. This commission is now sitting <pb facs="0541"
                        n="283" xml:id="pg283"/> in Stockholm in conjunction with a similar
                    commission appointed by the Swedish Government.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson Caffery</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
